    - target: {fileID: 3638083915130247541, guid: e11acd7e824adcc43a4715c4f5daa2ba,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: 'This example demonstrates and prescribes preferred methods for using
        the meshing functionality.

        Provided is a MeshingExample script that
        drives parameters of the meshing API through the MeshingSubsystemComponent.


        This
        example provides a use case of the MapEvents functionality, clearing all
        fragments and refreshing the mesh when a new map is detected.

        It
        uses Unity''s default ARMeshManager to drive the meshing subsystem.


        The
        scene provides several examples of changing the way rendering and physics
        interact with the meshing results. You can:

        - Visualize the mesh
        results. Each setting demonstrates the different parameters used for tweaking
        the mesh detector

        - Shoot prefab spheres into the scene for physics
        interaction.


        <color=#B7B7B8><b>Mandatory permissions required by
        this feature</b></color>

        - SpatialMapping'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 3981727701387534120, guid: e11acd7e824adcc43a4715c4f5daa2ba,
        type: 3}
